# multiACE: let Klipper (user lava) open USB-RS485 dongles that drive an
# MMU (CFS Nano on a CH340, ACE 2 on a generic adapter). Without it the
# tty is root:dialout 0660 and lava is not in dialout. The rule matches
# every CH340, so it keeps root:dialout access: a host without a lava user
# (generic Klipper, CH340 mainboard) stays at its usual root:dialout 0660.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", OWNER="lava", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
